  <section class="summary" aria-labelledby="sum">
    <h2 id="sum">The 30 second version</h2>
    <div><span class="k">Problem</span><p>The app shows status when the passenger needs a decision. So they leave and check somewhere else.</p></div>
    <div><span class="k">Decision</span><p>One hub that changes state across the journey, always answering a single question: what do I do now.</p></div>
    <div><span class="k">The one metric that matters</span><p>Not engagement, but a drop in refresh frequency. If people stop compulsively checking, the app has started doing the worrying for them.</p></div>
    <div><span class="k">What I learned</span><p>Urgency and importance are different axes, and sorting by the wrong one is what buried the essentials.</p></div>
  </section>

